		MultiHead(Q,K,V) = W_OY + Broadcast_{hd_V}(b_O^\top)
	\end{gathered}
	\label{att eq 4}
\end{equation}<|CIT-MASK|><|CIT-MASK|>

This concatenation step combines the independently attended features from each head into a single matrix, effectively mixing the different learned representations from each head.

In the multi-head attention<|CIT-MASK|>, the single-headed attention<|CIT-MASK|> is ran for $h$ heads, leading to a runtime of $\mathcal{O}(hn^2(d_K+d_V)) \in \mathcal{O}(n^2)$.

